<title>CANADA: Petro-Can cements Norsk deal.</title>
<headline>Petro-Can cements Norsk deal.</headline>
<dateline>ST. JOHN'S, Newfoundland 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petro-Canada said on Thursday it had formed a long-term strategic alliance with Norway's Norsk Hydro to pursue offshore oil and gas exploration in the Grand Banks region of Newfoundland.</p>
<p>The alliance, which first took effect on January 1, 1996, also gives Petro-Canada a working interest in two Norwegian oil fields in the North Sea.</p>
<p>&quot;Exploring for and developing oil reserves in the Grand Banks is one of Petro-Canada's core businesses,&quot; said Norm McIntyre, Petro-Canada's executive vice-president.</p>
</text>
